{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104178","id":2395400046,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Oxudu","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104178","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104178.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104178.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104178","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104178/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104178/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104178/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b4f6663afa58f897da69ebbf46a93bcd2747bee7","number":104178,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Recycle `zstd` decompression context if possible, avoiding repeated allocations.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Today, I profiled allocations of tps demo.\r\nSomething peculiar caught my eye: zstd contexts made up for 3GB of allocations (and deallocations) throughout the launch! I rewrote the code to re-use the instance, reducing allocations massively and speeding up the game's launch time slightly.\r\n\r\nAll in all, this PR saves 3GB (30%) of allocations and deallocations of a tps-demo launch. This amounts to a tiny average of 0.006s improvement (0.34%) of the game's launch time. Even with such small speed gains, think it's worth it because it means far less memory may be churned by the OS, which should improve general system load.\r\nTo pay for it, only one `zstd` stream can be decompressed at once. In addition, the pointer to it will stay in memory. Napkin math suggests it's about 100kb.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nI launched tps-demo and started the game. Upon successful launch, I immediately quit.\r\n\r\nI profiled total allocations using Apple Instruments.\r\nI inverted the call tree and found these top entries:\r\n```\r\n3304.22 MB      32.2%\t35245\t \tZSTD_customMalloc\r\n2086.02 MB      20.3%\t3054587\t \tMemory::alloc_static(unsigned long, bool)\r\n1900.39 MB      18.5%\t17745619\t \t_malloc_type_malloc_outlined\r\n 659.83 MB       6.4%\t466\t \tIOGPUResourceCreate\r\n```\r\n\r\nI implemented a very crude caching strategy that reuses the context as long as the parameters don't change. The instance will be lazily created on first zstd decompression, so it won't burden applications not using zstd.\r\nI'm guessing the reallocation isn't necessary _at all_, technically. Somebody confirm it isn't and I will just set the parameter instead of reallocating on changes.\r\n\r\nAfter my changes, the zstd entry disappears:\r\n```\r\n2099.70 MB      31.9%\t3148754\t \tMemory::alloc_static(unsigned long, bool)\r\n1733.48 MB      26.3%\t15592696\t \t_malloc_type_malloc_outlined\r\n 460.56 MB       7.0%\t458\t \tIOGPUResourceCreate\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Alternatives\r\n\r\nIt may be possible to cache a `Compression` instance in `ResourceLoaderBinary`, which is almost entirely the sole cause of decompression calls:\r\n```\r\n3304.22 MB      32.2%\t35245\t \tZSTD_customMalloc\r\n3304.22 MB      32.2%\t35245\t \t Compression::decompress(unsigned char*, int, unsigned char const*, int, Compression::Mode)\r\n3005.72 MB      29.2%\t32061\t \t  FileAccessCompressed::get_buffer(unsigned char*, unsigned long long) const\r\n2942.06 MB      28.6%\t31382\t \t   ResourceLoaderBinary::parse_variant(Variant&)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTheoretically, this could save us from needing to keep a zstd instance in memory forever.\r\nHowever, I don't see `ResourceLoaderBinary` being unloaded either, so it wouldn't really change anything. So I opted for the simple method and just keep zstd loaded statically.\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://a